CM ============================================================
CM 4-Element Square Phased Array — 20M (14.175 MHz)
CM TM-HYB-001 Rev A
CM
CM Four half-wave dipoles at corners of a λ/2 × λ/2 square.
CM Sequential phase shift: 0°, 90°, 180°, 270° (cardioid rotational symmetry)
CM
CM Layout (top view, Z=10m):
CM
CM   El.1(0°)      El.4(270°)
CM   (0,0)         (10.58,0)
CM
CM   El.2(90°)     El.3(180°)
CM   (0,10.58)     (10.58,10.58)
CM
CM λ/2 spacing = c/(2×14.175MHz) = 10.584 m
CM
CM Feed network:
CM   4-way Wilkinson to each element
CM   90° all-pass networks for sequential phase shift:
CM     El.1: 0° (reference)
CM     El.2: −90° (one all-pass section)
CM     El.3: −180° (two all-pass sections)
CM     El.4: −270° (three all-pass sections)
CM
CM This creates a broadside array with circular symmetry.
CM Pattern: bidirectional broadside beam (perpendicular to array plane)
CM Alternatively: use Wilkinson + quadrature hybrids for rotating beam.
CM ============================================================
CM === ELEMENT 1 (0°) at (0, 0, 10) ===
CM === ELEMENT 2 (−90°) at (0, 10.584, 10) ===
CM === ELEMENT 3 (−180°) at (10.584, 10.584, 10) ===
CM === ELEMENT 4 (−270°) at (10.584, 0, 10) ===
CM === GROUND: Average ===
CM === EXCITATIONS (sequential phase, equal amplitude) ===
CM PHASE ENCODING:
CM  El.1:  1.0+j0.0   = 1∠0°
CM  El.2:  0.0−j1.0   = 1∠−90°
CM  El.3: −1.0+j0.0   = 1∠−180°
CM  El.4:  0.0+j1.0   = 1∠−270° = 1∠+90°
CM === FREQUENCY ===
CM === RADIATION PATTERNS ===
CM Full azimuth/elevation pattern
CM Azimuth at 20° elevation (DX angle)
CM ============================================================
CM EXPECTED RESULTS (broadside pattern):
CM   Gain: ≈ 8 dBi (≈6 dBd) above average ground at 20°
CM   Array factor: +6 dB over single dipole (4 elements)
CM   Pattern: figure-8 broadside (two main lobes up and down if
CM            array lies in horizontal plane)
CM
CM ENDFIRE VARIANT:
CM   Change elements to vertical dipoles or verticals.
CM   Array produces endfire beam in +Y or +X direction depending
CM   on phase progression direction.
CM   For vertical endfire: Δφ=90° per λ/4 spacing → unidirectional.
CM
CM BEAM STEERING:
CM   To steer beam in azimuth, change phase progression:
CM     North beam:   0°, −90°, −180°, −270°
CM     East beam:    0°, +90°, +180°, +270° (reverse)
CM     Use PIN diode phase shifters or relay-switched all-pass networks.
CM
CM PHASING NETWORK (see TM-HYB-001 sch_lumped_element_hf.txt):
CM   All-pass 90° section for 14.175 MHz:
CM     L = 50/(2π×14.175e6) = 561 nH (T-50-6, 9t, #22 AWG)
CM     C = 1/(2π×14.175e6×50) = 225 pF (C0G)
CM   Three cascaded sections give 270° shift for El.4.
CM ============================================================
